pythia.lucifertotem.nothing=I see nothing near. The sea is wide.
sibyl.lucifertotem.title=The Leaves of the Sibyl. Read them where the wind cannot reach.
sibyl.lucifertotem.page=%s
sibyl.lucifertotem.verse.1=The purple comes from the sea; the sea comes from the star.
sibyl.lucifertotem.verse.2=Who sips the venom daily, the venom fears.
sibyl.lucifertotem.verse.3=Three circles, the west wind, and the root comes quietly.
sibyl.lucifertotem.verse.4=She who looks back turns to stone; look into bronze instead.
sibyl.lucifertotem.verse.5=Below the honey, the snakes; below the snakes, the truth.
sibyl.lucifertotem.verse.6=Three sisters sing, and the morning star bows its head.
sibyl.lucifertotem.verse.7=The old ram enters the cauldron; a lamb comes out.
sibyl.lucifertotem.verse.8=Thirst that no bread can quench, vinegar can.
sibyl.lucifertotem.end=The rest the wind has taken.

